#: includes/Admin_Page.php:409
msgid "Claims about implemented features, integrations, customer usage, benchmark quality, ranking impact, or availability must be confirmed by the operator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin_Page.php:411
msgid ""
"Titles should include the main topic keyword and avoid clickbait.\n"
"Descriptions should state the problem, audience, and core conclusion.\n"
"Use clear headings, steps, caveats, and engineering boundary notes.\n"
"Prefer internal links to related tutorials, architecture notes, and tool reviews."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin_Page.php:412
msgid ""
"Start with a direct answer, then add conditions, steps, and limits.\n"
"Prefer FAQ, short definitions, comparison tables, and actionable checklists.\n"
"Avoid abstract-only answers; include practical guidance."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin_Page.php:413
msgid ""
"Make key conclusions clear, standalone, and easy for AI systems to summarize.\n"
"Define important terms when they first appear.\n"
"Distinguish implemented features, development-stage behavior, and future plans.\n"
"Avoid inflated claims; state boundaries, inputs, outputs, and limits."
msgstr ""

